window.docContents[252].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Security.Binary/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Security___Binary":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Specifications/Security › Binary.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 38 of 85 lines trusted source ↗trust banner in the header: B1, trusted: the statement; the closure computes B2 for the symbolic proofRead the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\n\n\nBinary Security Statement for libsignal-cliTrusted: the statement.States the top-level security theorem SignalSessionSecurePlaced bytes (and placement-indexed SignalSessionSecurePlacedAt mpl mmpl bytes) for the ARM64 ELF binary implementing PQXDH, SPQR, and the Triple Ratchet, via the run-parametric property SignalSessionSecureFor Agree R.\n\n\n\ndef SignalSessionSecureForL44–67 ↗#Protocol security over run relation R and primitive-agreement predicate Agree from initDirs: for every valid interp, agreeing W, and well-formed r, there exist opaque semantics S such that every guarded, coin-fresh trace evs is either explained (Explains) and satisfies AllSecurityQueriesHoldOnHwTrace, or has an explained prefix evs₁ satisfying AllSecurityQueriesHoldOnHwTrace whose next run event hits NextEventCollides.\n\ndef SignalSessionSecurePlacedAtL69–75 ↗#Security and no-fault progress of ELF image bytes at placements (mpl, mmpl): parses bytes, verifies CliElfCodeMatchesPlaced mpl mmpl elf and CliElfProgressPlaced mpl mmpl elf, and asserts SignalSessionSecureFor HooksMatchInterpretation (elfRelPlaced mpl mmpl elf).\n\ndef SignalSessionSecurePlacedL77–86 ↗#Relocatable binary security quantified over all valid placements (mpl, mmpl) of libsignalSessionLib and mallocngLib in bytes.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Specifications/Security/Binary.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Security.Binary/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Security___Binary"}});